{
  "title": "82: al-Infetaar الإنفطار",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِذَا السَّمَآءُ انْفَطَرَتْۙ‏(1)\nEZAS SAMAAA-UN FATARAT.\nWhen the heavens cleave asunder\nوَاِذَا الْكَوَاكِبُ انْتَثَرَتْۙ‏(2)\nWA EZAL KAWAAKEBUN TASARAT.\nAnd When the stars disperse\nوَاِذَا الْبِحَارُ فُجِّرَتْۙ‏(3)\nWA EZAL BEHAARO FUJJERAT.\nAnd When the seas be comingled\nوَاِذَا الْقُبُوْرُ بُعْثِرَتْۙ‏(4)\nWA EZAL QOBOORO BO’SERAT.\nAnd when the graves be overturned (to be vacated)\nعَلِمَتْ نَفْسٌ مَّا قَدَّمَتْ وَاَخَّرَتْؕ‏(5)\nA’LEMAT NAFSUM MAA QADDAMAT WA AKHKHARAT.\nThen shall every soul know what it hath sent forth and left behind\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْاِنْسَانُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ الْكَرِيْمِۙ‏(6)\nYAA AYYOHAL INSAANO MAA GHARRAKA BE-RABBEKAL KAREEMIL.\nO’ thou man! What hath beguiled thee from thy Lord, the Most Gracious One\nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَكَ فَسَوّٰٮكَ فَعَدَلَكَۙ‏(7)\nLAZEE KHALAQAKA FA-SAWWAAKA FA-A’DALAKA.\n(He) Who created thee, and fashioned thee and (gave thee a body) justly proportioned\nفِىْۤ اَىِّ صُوْرَةٍ مَّا شَآءَ رَكَّبَكَؕ‏(8)\nFEE AYYE SOORATIM MAA SHAAA-A RAKKABAK.\nIn whatsoever form He willeth He casteth thee\nكَلَّا بَلْ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ بِالدِّيْنِۙ‏(9)\nKALLAA BAL TOKAZZEBOONA BID-DEENE.\nNay! but ye belie the Reckoning\nوَاِنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ لَحٰفِظِيْنَۙ‏(10)\nWA INNA A’LAYKUM LA-HAAFEZEENA.\nWhile verily over you are posted the Watchers\nكِرَامًا كَاتِبِيْنَۙ‏(11)\nKERAAMAN KAATEBEENA.\nRecorders Honourable\nيَعْلَمُوْنَ مَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(12)\nYA’LAMOONA MAA TAF-A’LOON.\nKnow they whatever ye do\nاِنَّ الْاَبْرَارَ لَفِىْ نَعِيْمٍۚ‏(13)\nINNAL ABRAARA LAFEE NA-E’EM.\nVerily, the righteous shall be amidst bounteous bliss\nوَاِنَّ الْفُجَّارَ لَفِىْ جَحِيْمٍ ۚۖ‏(14)\nWA INNAL FUJJAARA LAFEE JAHEEMIN-Y.\nAnd verily the wicked shall be in the flaming fire\nيَّصْلَوْنَهَا يَوْمَ الدِّيْنِ‏(15)\nYASLAWNAHAA YAWMAD DEEN.\nThey shall be committed to it on the Day of Judgment\nوَمَا هُمْ عَنْهَا بِغَآئِبِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nWA MAA HUM A’NHAA BE-GHAAA-EBEEN.\nNor they shall themselves be absent from it\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(17)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUD DEENE.\nAnd what will make thee know what the Day of Judgment shall be?\nثُمَّ مَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(18)\nSUMMA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUD DEEN.\nThen what maketh thee know what the Day of Judgment is?\nيَوْمَ لَا تَمْلِكُ نَفْسٌ لِّنَفْسٍ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَالْاَمْرُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلَّهِ‏(19)\nYAWMA LAA TAMLEKO NAFSUL LE-NAFSIN SHAY-AA, WAL AMRO YAWMA-EZIL LILLAAH.\n(It is) The day on which soul shall own not anything (helpful) for another soul; and the Command Supreme that day shall be God’s (alone)",
  "merits": "Surah al-Infetaar (The Cleaving Asunder)\nThere are 19 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that if a person recites this Surah frequently in his prayers then on the Day of Judgement there will be no curtain between Allah (s.w.t.) and himself and when his book of deeds will be opened, Allah (s.w.t.) will protect him from humiliation.\nIf a prisoner writes this Surah and keeps it with him, he will be released sooner and he will be saved from any dangers. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that even if the sins of the one who recites this Surah are equal to the drops of rain, he will still be forgiven. This Surah is also good for the eyes and one should blow gently into the eyes after reciting this Surah."
